 "text": "Plowing is a ritual activity. The act of plowing a field prepares the land for spring seed. It often marks the first arrival of a people in a new land, so the invaders of Ireland are said to clear and plow different parts. Gods or heroes usually do the plowing, though goddesses appear. The harvest god Crom Dubh is also called Soicin, meaning little plow, and Mac Cecht, husband of Fódla, means plowman.",
